WEBVTT

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.580
Oh, Yutoria!

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.200
B-Big news!

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.040
Wh-What are you so worked up about?

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.160
I...!

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.450
I?

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.870
I...

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.660
I made a juicy discovery!

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.910
A juicy discovery?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.660
"Episode Four: Treasure Hunt"

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.000
"Episode Four: Treasure Hunt"
When I hear juicy,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.370
I immediately think of roast boar
and maju seafood soup!

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.450
I doubt she's talking about juicy food, Sis.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:17.950
Would you shut up? You don't think I know?!

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.830
So, what's this juicy discovery?

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.790
I-It's this!

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:23.790
Hmm?

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.120
Th-This is... a treasure map?!

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:33.410
Yes! If we find the treasure,
we could probably pay off the inheritance tax!

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.000
That does sound pretty juicy!

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.580
But, how did you...?

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.540
I got it from an acquaintance. Um--

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.750
It's me who found it!

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.580
Y-You're...?

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:50.620
I'm Marika, the most adorable,
genius wizard of our time!

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.580
Genius, huh?

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:57.830
She's only like ten, right?
For being that tiny, she sure is arrogant...

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.330
Hold up! You just thought I'm tiny, didn't you?!

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:02.080
Ack!

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.040
And arrogant too, right?!

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.750
I wasn't thinking that!

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.120
She's pretty sharp...

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.200
I met Marika while working on a job a while back.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.330
She knows lots about magic,

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:18.830
and graduated from Adventure Tech
by skipping grades!

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.950
Yeah? That's impressive!

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:26.160
Call me Queen Marika!
Get on your knees and lick my feet!

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.540
H-Her personality could use some work though...

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.450
So, you found this map?

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:37.450
That's right! We can find the treasure
together and split it up!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:42.500
There you have it, President!
We've got ourselves a treasure hunt!

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.950
A treasure hunt, huh?
That reminds me of back when--

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.700
Awesome! I love stuff like this!

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.160
But, Sis... Don't we have
that other thing today?

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.870
Oh, right!

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:00.450
I like your enthusiasm,
but we can't wait around.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.330
Someone might find it before we do.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.790
Good point.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:08.620
President, you better find it
in my place, or else!

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.750
O-Or else what?

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:14.790
This is our big chance to pay off
the inheritance tax!

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.250
You gotta find the treasure, no matter what!

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.500
Right... Talk about pressure...

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:26.080
What's the deal with your president?
He doesn't seem reliable to me.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.870
N-Not even the kid trusts me...

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:35.700
It'll be fine! I'll be there too,
and he always pulls through when it matters!

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.080
Probably...

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:42.450
Even my childhood friend
secretary has doubts, but...

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:46.160
No need to worry! I'll bring back the treasure!

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.870
You can count on me, guys!

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:53.330
Having said that, where do we
even start the search?

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:58.700
Um, it says "Dig between the antlers
of the green maze."

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.160
I wonder where the green maze is.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:05.290
Maybe it's the Rurud Forest
on the outskirts of town?

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:08.000
It's known for people getting lost.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.330
Oh, that might be it!

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.750
Not sure if I'm right though.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:17.000
I basically have zero faith in you,
but let's check it out.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:21.000
You didn't have to say it aloud.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.750
What? Say something?!

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.370
No, not at all!

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:29.700
What?! You're all sold out?!

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:34.660
I'm sorry. Limited-edition stuff goes quick.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:41.040
And here I saved all that money and brought
my brother to carry stuff home!

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.620
It's kind of shocking that you love cute stuff.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.450
Argh, sheesh!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.580
I should've just gone on the treasure hunt!

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.500
Leaving those two in charge worries me.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:01.580
Say, I've been wondering...
How does Yutoria know the president?

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.910
I don't know the whole story,

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:10.250
but I guess the old man took Yutoria in
since she didn't have relatives.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:15.200
When they were young,
they basically grew up like siblings.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:20.500
I mentioned it earlier, but didn't we go
on a treasure hunt years ago?

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.000
Oh! You remember that too?

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.500
--Check this out!
--Yeah. We were exploring the office
when we discovered a map.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.000
--Whoa!
--Yeah. We were exploring the office
when we discovered a map.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.450
--Let's go, Minato!
--You wanted to keep searching till we found it.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.950
--Wait up!
--You wanted to keep searching till we found it.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:36.500
And we ended up not getting home
until well past dark.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.580
My dad was so mad at us.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.000
That's right.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.250
We never found it in the end though.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.580
I wonder what that map was.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.330
Hey! Spare me the sappy stories!

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:52.000
I-It's not sappy!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.250
It's not like that!

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:58.410
Whatever the case, we're here now.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:00.950
So this is the Rurud Forest...

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:04.910
It's so dense in here, it really is like a maze.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.620
But, I wonder what the antlers are.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.290
Maybe we'll see horns somewhere.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.870
By the way, Marika. Where did you get this map?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.870
My adventurer grandpa had it in his cellar.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:23.830
Won't he know something
about it if we asked him?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.450
I'm afraid we can't.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.330
He died about a year ago.

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:31.080
S-Sorry.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.660
It's okay. He lived to 120
and passed away peacefully.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:39.040
Anyways, let's hurry and look for those antlers!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.950
Sure, but where do we even start?

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:44.750
Huh? It's you guys again!

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.910
Oh! You're...!

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.040
I'm willing to pay.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:57.040
Thomas! Long time no see!
Did your sister like the present?

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.950
Yeah! She was super happy with it!

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.370
That's wonderful!

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:05.040
So? What are you guys doing way out here?

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.450
About that... Do you know
what the "antlers" are?

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:14.200
Oh, the antlers?
Everyone from around here knows the place.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.120
Huh?

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.910
It's these two trees down yonder.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:21.700
Really? If it's not much trouble,
could you take us there?

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.910
Hold up!

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:26.410
You're gonna rely on this brat?

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:29.950
How am I a brat? We're practically the same age!

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.540
Well, how old are you?

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.830
I'm ten.

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:36.950
That makes me two years older than you.
Call me Queen Marika.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:38.410
So, Marika...

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.950
--Queen Marika!
--Ow!

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:43.160
Whoa! V-Violence is bad!

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:45.790
Man, what a violent girl!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:46.910
Hmph!

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:50.000
Anyways, could you show us the way?

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.000
Sure! Leave it to me! It's this way!

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:59.660
What a blockhead.
We'll never find the treasure like this.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:02.450
Whoa! It's a treasure, Sis!

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:05.200
By treasure, you mean mushrooms?

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.830
Uh, did you touch it?

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.370
I-Is that bad?

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:13.250
H-Huh?! What's this awful smell?!

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:18.620
Anything that touches a hook-nosed mushroom
will hold its smell for days!

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.830
What part of that is a treasure?!

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:25.120
B-Because it's a mushroom
that rarely pops up on the market!

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:29.750
They're incredibly tasty to eat!
As long as you plug your nose!

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.330
How can you taste if you're plugging your nose?!

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.950
So these are the antlers...

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.290
It kinda does resemble some.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.120
Hey, find anything yet?

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:46.160
H-Hold on! I'm still digging!

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.450
Are these really the antlers?

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:53.080
I told you!
These are the only antlers in the forest!

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.000
Oh! I found something!

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.200
The treasure?!

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.250
Hurry! Dig it out!

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.540
R-Right!

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.410
Is this the treasure?

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.120
It's smaller than I thought it'd be.

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.000
Maybe there's jewels in it.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:11.500
Jeez! Stop making us wait and open it!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.040
S-Sorry.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:17.540
It's... a note?

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:19.540
What does it say?

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:24.160
Um... "Look at the picture
deep in the haunted house."

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:27.750
It's a hint on how to reach the next clue!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.750
See? Told you so!

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:32.500
Hmph! It's just a coincidence.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:37.370
But really, thanks.
We couldn't have found it without you.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.250
No problem! Don't mention it!

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:45.290
More importantly, mind if I come
along on your treasure hunt?

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.200
Huh?

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.660
It seems kinda fun!

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.250
Can I? You'll be glad to have me!

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.250
You might be right, but...

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.950
It's settled then!

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.950
Like I said: a brat.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.620
Wait, Thomas!

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:03.370
We're supposed to find a picture
in some haunted house.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.370
Do you know what that means?

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:09.000
It's gotta be the abandoned house nearby.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.540
The kids around here call it a haunted house.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.330
Huh? You knew that too?

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:16.250
Yup! It's this way!

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:20.830
Argh, this totally stinks!

00:11:20.830 --> 00:11:25.330
Yeah. I knew they were expensive,
but that much for a mushroom?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.450
Not that! The smell on my hands!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:32.410
Don't you worry!
I've got something good for you!

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:33.410
Huh?

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.500
Ta-da!

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.370
Guide?!

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:38.080
How did you just...?!

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.580
It's a special skill, "Shadow Step."

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:44.910
I happened to spot you two,
so I thought I'd surprise you!

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:47.290
Here, take this!

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:52.910
Haunted by a nasty smell?
Use this ghost deodorizer spray!

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:55.750
Um, thank you very much.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:59.540
Weren't you going on
the treasure hunt with the others?

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.950
I was busy handling an emergency deposit.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:08.410
Also, I didn't want to get in the way
of Yutoria and the president reminiscing.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.040
Reminiscing?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:16.040
I've worked at Kibou Company for so long,
there's certain things I know.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.910
Y-You sure are a mysterious one...

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:23.120
Yeah... Could you maybe not
use special skills in town?

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.910
This is the haunted house?

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:32.540
Yup! This abandoned house!

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:41.500
To think there was an abandoned
house here... I had no idea.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:45.830
Really? All the kids that
play around here know about it.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:46.950
Ack!

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:50.330
By the way, where do you live, Marika?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.450
I told you to call me Queen Marika!

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:57.500
Good grief. My house is on top
of that hill nearby.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:02.250
Dang, that's really close!
And you've never been to the haunted house?

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.750
What's it matter?

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:06.370
I've got it! You don't have friends!

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:08.660
Th-That's not true!

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:11.410
By that reaction, I bet I'm right!

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:15.870
Shut up! Who cares?! I don't need any friends!

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.200
Such a loner!

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.330
--I-I am not a loner!
--Looks like they're getting along well now.

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:20.250
--No need to hide it!
--Looks like they're getting along well now.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:20.950
--No need to hide it!
--Yeah. I'm glad they're having fun.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.700
--I'm not hiding anything!
--Yeah. I'm glad they're having fun.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:25.540
Soon enough, the treasure will be ours!

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:29.370
Y-Yeah... Your eyes are scaring me though.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.830
So this is the haunted house?

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:51.410
Sure is dark since nobody lives here.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.290
Everyone watch where you're going!

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.080
Ow, ow, ow!

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.750
You okay, Yutoria?!

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.450
I-I'm not okay!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:04.620
What now? It doesn't seem safe to keep walking.

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:08.580
Jeez, you're hopeless without me.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:10.700
Whoa! It's bright now!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.410
I used light magic on it. Now we can keep going.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:18.330
Awesome! Your staff is glowing!
Lemme see! Lemme touch it!

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:21.000
Hold up! Keep your hands to yourself!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:25.160
Ouch! But still, you're pretty amazing, Marika!

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:28.700
You're only noticing now?
And call me Queen Marika!

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.580
You wanna be an adventurer?

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:31.580
Huh?

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:39.000
That's right. That's been my dream
for as long as I've known.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:45.250
I wanted to be a great and respected wizard,
just like my grandpa.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:48.790
Yeah? Your grandpa sounds cool.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:52.200
He was. And I loved him.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.830
Ouch!

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:57.370
What the heck!
Why put a wall right after a turn?!

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:02.330
What gives? It's locked...

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.200
I think it's the only way we can go.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:08.250
Should I ask it to open nicely with my foot?

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:11.870
Wait! The whole house might
collapse if you do that.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:14.000
T-True...

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.330
Hmm, what to do...?

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.910
Oh! I found a hole!

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:21.370
I can crawl through and open it!

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:22.410
Really?

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:25.540
Yeah, but it's pitch black over there.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.410
Does this help at all?

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:30.330
Huh? Thank you!

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:32.120
Here goes nothing!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.250
There, it's open!

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.950
Thanks, Thomas!

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.080
That was a piece of cake!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.250
I'm really glad the two of you came along.

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:52.160
You should be! It's not every day
you meet a genius like me!

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:55.200
Yeah. Thanks for the help, you two.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:01.750
Eww, you're creeping me out.
Come on, let's keep moving!

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:09.250
Oh? President and Yutoria went on a
treasure hunt when they were young?

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:13.660
Yeah. At least, that's what I heard
from the old man.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:18.870
They put their minds together
and searched with all their hearts!

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:23.750
They would've been roughly
the same age as Marika is today.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.950
Are we getting near the end?

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:28.620
Probably. Try to keep up with me.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:29.750
Okay!

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:31.290
Hmm...

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.290
Something wrong, President?

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:36.500
No. But the way this has progressed,

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:41.040
it's almost like someone
set this up for those two.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:45.580
Now that you mention it, kinda.
Maybe it's a coincidence?

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:48.660
Anyways, let's hurry and find the treasure!

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:52.330
Look. This is as far as we can go.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:55.830
In that case, there's nowhere else to look.

00:16:55.830 --> 00:17:01.330
The clue says, "Look at the picture
deep in the haunted house."

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.950
You think that's it?

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:08.370
Wait! There's something there!

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:09.620
H-Huh?

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:14.370
Maju in a place like this?!

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:18.080
There shouldn't be maju this close to the city!

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.700
As I thought... Could it be...?!

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:26.080
Now that it's come to this, stay back, you two!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.370
This is nothing.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:28.410
What?!

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:31.200
Marika the great is about to destroy you!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.410
I-In just one blow...

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:51.200
Impressed? Fire magic works
really well against ghost maju!

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:54.000
Wow! Magic is so cool!

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:57.120
The danger has been slain!

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:59.500
Now, let's inspect this picture!

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:04.830
Oh? There's something here!

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:07.040
This is... a letter?

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.620
A letter? That's the treasure?

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.870
I don't know.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.290
Huh?

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:15.450
Wh-What it is, Yutoria?

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:19.250
The letter says, "To my dearest Marika."

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:21.870
Huh? Why does it have my name?

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:28.620
This is...

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.370
"To my dearest Marika.

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:37.700
If you're reading this letter,
it means that I'm no longer in this world.

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:42.410
I lived a very long life
and parted without regret.

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:46.330
However, there is one thing that concerns me.

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:50.250
That would be you, Marika.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:53.200
You were always such a clever girl.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:57.700
Because of that, your life
was full of adults like me,

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:00.910
thus, you didn't have any friends your age."

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:08.160
--Grandpa! Bye-bye!
--"Of course, while I'm incredibly proud
that you wish to follow in my footsteps,

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:15.000
...to a greater extent, I worry that it means
you won't make any friends.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:19.160
Which is why I left behind a treasure map.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:24.330
I planned it so you couldn't reach
the treasure all on your own.

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:28.700
It will take your magic and
the knowledge of a local child.

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:34.660
Only by working together will you
be able to discover the treasure.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:40.040
I hope this helps you find the
most priceless treasure of all."

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:43.870
"To my dearest Marika..."

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:51.500
Wh-What gives? I never cared
about not having friends.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.660
I was happy just having you, Grandpa.

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:56.500
Marika...

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.450
Sorry.

00:19:58.450 --> 00:19:59.950
Thank you.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:09.290
Hey. Your grandpa wanted you
to make friends, right?

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:11.370
And what about it?

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:15.250
Then it's all good,
because you and I are friends now!

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:16.950
Wha...?!

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:19.160
We're friends, right?

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:25.080
W-Who do you think you are?!
I said I don't need any friends!

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.410
But we already are.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:29.700
We're friends now.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.910
Friends...

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:34.080
Yup! Friends!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.750
So let's get along, Marika!

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:42.040
I-I told you to call me Queen Marika.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:54.450
Good for those two.

00:20:54.450 --> 00:21:00.000
Yeah. It's a shame there wasn't a real treasure,
but it sure warmed my heart.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:06.830
There's nothing quite like a treasure hunt
to bring a couple kids together.

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:09.620
Do you think, back then...?

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.250
Back then?

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:15.790
You know, the treasure hunt we did as kids.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:18.830
It was around the time you first moved in.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:24.120
Now that you mention it, we were kinda
distant and awkward to start.

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:29.620
Maybe my dad left out that map
so we'd find it and grow closer.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:31.700
Just like Marika's grandpa.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:35.790
If you're right,
I'm grateful the old man did that.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:38.370
It helped the two of us bond.

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:42.410
True, but he also got mad at us
for coming home late.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.910
That sounds like something he'd do.

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:51.620
The most priceless treasure of all, huh?

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:04.700
Yeah... I'm sure he meant
the treasure of friendship.

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:07.950
President!

00:22:07.950 --> 00:22:09.580
Oh, guys!

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:16.330
How was it?! Where's the treasure?
Did you rake in a fortune?!

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:18.910
Uh, well... About that...
